  "data": {
    "id": "ovc",
    "name": "Outer vacuum can (OVC)",
    "category": "vacuum",
    "parent": "top_plate_300K",
    "function": "Brushed stainless-steel can sealed to the top plate by an O-ring under a 48-bolt flange; it holds the insulating vacuum (below 1e-5 mbar cold). Without it, gas conduction and convection would dump kilowatts into the 50 K stage. The dished (2:1 ellipsoidal) base resists the 1 bar external load. Its pressure is the first quantity checked before starting a cooldown and the first to move when a leak or a warm-up begins.",
